  "description": "State College 160-episode staged curriculum with exactly 2500 individual pedestrians. Stage E learns natural environment dynamics, stage A learns decision-interval installation effects, and stage F jointly learns the dedicated NMCC continuation value by backward returns across all eight sequential installations. Every episode starts with two shelters, installs eight equal 270-person shelters at t=15,30,...,120, continues through t=180, and provides 2700 total places. Exploration, entropy, temperature, and actor/critic learning rates reset and decay independently within every stage. The signed learning reward compares the chosen shelter with the uniform feasible random-site average; deterministic matched evaluation uses realised hazard-weighted time to safety.",
